cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below. Not peer reviewed. Produced by AI models under the direction of the repository owner (see AI_DISCLOSURE.md)."
title: "Five points on the sphere, Riesz s = 2: one exact three-point certificate"
type: software
authors:
  - name: alejandrozarco
repository-code: "https://github.com/alejandrozarco/five-points-riesz2"
abstract: >-
  An exact rational three-point semidefinite-programming certificate, with an independent exact checker, that the
  triangular bipyramid uniquely minimises the Riesz s = 2 energy of five distinct points on the unit sphere. The
  theorem is known (Schwartz); the lower bound is a single sharp three-point certificate without case analysis; uniqueness uses a finite Gram-matrix enumeration. AI-produced;
  not peer reviewed.
keywords:
  - Riesz energy
  - Thomson problem
  - triangular bipyramid
  - semidefinite programming
  - three-point bound
  - computer-checked certificate
license: Apache-2.0
